# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding for the latest version of Qiskit bosons"
msgstr "Simulasikan dinamik Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan pengekodan untuk versi terkini boson Qiskit"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding"
msgstr "Simulasikan dinamik Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan pengekodan"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-getting-started\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding {#simulate-bose-hubbard-dynamics-with-a-choice-of-encoding}"
msgstr "Simulasikan dinamik Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan pengekodan {#simulate-bose-hubbard-dynamics-with-a-choice-of-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide builds a circuit for the **time dynamics of the one-dimensional Bose-Hubbard model**, from writing down the Hamiltonian to checking the evolved site densities against an exact reference. What makes the route interesting is a single idea:\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini membina litar untuk **dinamik masa model Bose-Hubbard satu dimensi**, daripada menulis Hamiltonian hingga menyemak ketumpatan tapak yang telah berkembang terhadap rujukan tepat. Apa yang menjadikan laluan ini menarik ialah satu idea:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Do not choose a boson-to-qubit encoding when you build the circuit. Build the circuit on **bosonic modes**, and let the **transpiler** decide how those modes become qubits.\n"
msgstr "> Jangan pilih pengekodan boson-ke-qubit semasa anda membina litar. Bina litar pada **mod bosonik**, dan biarkan **Transpiler** menentukan bagaimana mod tersebut menjadi qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For bosons, you nearly always need to defer the encoding. A bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many particles, so its Fock space is infinite-dimensional and no encoding exists until you first pick a **truncation** $d$ (the number of occupation levels you keep). In code the truncation is given as the largest occupation a mode can hold, `max_occupation` $= d - 1$, so a mode that keeps the levels $0, 1, 2$ has `max_occupation = 2` and $d = 3$.\n"
msgstr "Bagi boson, anda hampir sentiasa perlu menangguhkan pengekodan. Satu mod bosonik memegang zarah sebanyak mana pun, jadi ruang Focknya berdimensi tak terhingga dan tiada pengekodan wujud sehingga anda memilih **pemangkasan** $d$ (bilangan aras penghunian yang anda kekalkan). Dalam kod, pemangkasan diberikan sebagai penghunian terbesar yang boleh dipegang oleh satu mod, `max_occupation` $= d - 1$, jadi satu mod yang mengekalkan aras $0, 1, 2$ mempunyai `max_occupation = 2` dan $d = 3$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That makes the truncation a *parameter of the encoding*, not of the physics, and it is a parameter you want to vary: too small and the answer is wrong, too large and the circuit is needlessly wide. If you defer the encoding to transpile time, you can sweep the truncation without changing the circuit, the Hamiltonian, or the grouping.\n"
msgstr "Itu menjadikan pemangkasan sebagai *parameter pengekodan*, bukan parameter fizik, dan ia ialah parameter yang anda mahu ubah: terlalu kecil dan jawapan salah, terlalu besar dan litar menjadi lebar tanpa keperluan. Jika anda menangguhkan pengekodan sehingga masa transpilasi, anda boleh menyapu pemangkasan tanpa mengubah litar, Hamiltonian, atau pengumpulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"See also\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [operators guide](operators#operators-explanation) for the operator data structure, the [mappers guide](mappers#mappers-explanation) for the encodings and the recipe for writing a custom mapper, and the [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) for the transpiler stages referenced throughout.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Lihat juga\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [Panduan operator](operators#operators-explanation) untuk struktur data operator, [panduan mapper](mappers#mappers-explanation) untuk pengekodan dan resipi menulis mapper tersuai, dan [panduan transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) untuk peringkat Transpiler yang dirujuk sepanjang panduan ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Truncation, and what it costs {#truncation-and-what-it-costs}"
msgstr "Pemangkasan, dan kosnya {#truncation-and-what-it-costs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you truncate a mode to $d$ levels, you break the canonical commutator on the highest retained level <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3), so no encoding is an isomorphism of *algebras*: a bosonic encoding maps states, and operators acting within the truncated subspace. Two consequences matter for everything that follows:\n"
msgstr "Apabila anda memangkas satu mod kepada $d$ aras, anda memecahkan komutator kanonik pada aras terakhir yang dikekalkan <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id3), jadi tiada pengekodan yang merupakan isomorfisme *aljabar*: satu pengekodan bosonik memetakan keadaan, dan operator yang bertindak dalam subruang terpangkas. Dua akibat penting untuk semua yang berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$d$ must bound the occupation reachable by the dynamics, not merely that of the initial state.\n"
msgstr "$d$ mesti membatasi penghunian yang boleh dicapai oleh dinamik, bukan sekadar penghunian keadaan awal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping does not commute with normal ordering, so decide once whether your Hamiltonian is defined in normal-ordered form, and stay consistent.\n"
msgstr "Pemetaan tidak berkomut dengan penertiban normal, jadi putuskan sekali sama ada Hamiltonian anda ditakrifkan dalam bentuk tertib normal, dan kekal konsisten.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [mappers guide](mappers#truncation-explanation) derives the defect and shows both consequences on running code.\n"
msgstr "[Panduan mapper](mappers#truncation-explanation) menerbitkan kecacatan itu dan menunjukkan kedua-dua akibat pada kod yang berjalan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-hamiltonian\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Hamiltonian {#1-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "1. Hamiltonian {#1-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Bose-Hubbard model on a lattice with bonds $\\langle i j \\rangle$ is\n"
msgstr "Model Bose-Hubbard pada kekisi dengan ikatan $\\langle i j \\rangle$ ialah\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{\\langle i j \\rangle} \\left(b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i\\right)\n"
"    + \\frac{U}{2} \\sum_i n_i (n_i - 1) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{\\langle i j \\rangle} \\left(b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i\\right)\n"
"    + \\frac{U}{2} \\sum_i n_i (n_i - 1) \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $n_i = b^\\dagger_i b_i$. The interaction counts *pairs* of bosons on a site, so it requires a site to hold two particles at once. Normal-ordered, $n_i(n_i-1) = b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, which is the form used in what follows.\n"
msgstr "dengan $n_i = b^\\dagger_i b_i$. Interaksi mengira *pasangan* boson pada satu tapak, jadi ia memerlukan satu tapak memegang dua zarah serentak. Dalam tertib normal, $n_i(n_i-1) = b^\\dagger_i b^\\dagger_i b_i b_i$, iaitu bentuk yang digunakan seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The geometry enters only through the edge list, so nothing is specific to a chain:\n"
msgstr "Geometri hanya masuk melalui senarai tepi, jadi tiada apa yang khusus kepada rantai:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two properties are worth checking first. The Hamiltonian must be Hermitian for $e^{-itH}$ to be unitary, and it conserves the total boson number:\n"
msgstr "Dua sifat patut disemak dahulu. Hamiltonian mesti Hermitian supaya $e^{-itH}$ unitari, dan ia mengekalkan jumlah bilangan boson:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the bosonic question: how many levels does this operator demand?\n"
msgstr "Sekarang soalan bosonik: berapa banyak aras yang dituntut oleh operator ini?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The interaction term applies two creation operators to one mode, so a mode has to hold two bosons for the term to act at all. That is a **maximum occupation** of 2, which is the number that [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") takes as its `max_occupation`. A mode that keeps the occupations $0, 1, 2$ has $d = \\texttt{max\\_occupation} + 1 = 3$ levels, so `max_occupation >= 2` is the same requirement as $d \\geq 3$.\n"
msgstr "Sebutan interaksi menggunakan dua operator penciptaan pada satu mod, jadi satu mod mesti memegang dua boson supaya sebutan itu bertindak sama sekali. Itu ialah **penghunian maksimum** sebanyak 2, iaitu nombor yang diambil oleh [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") sebagai `max_occupation`nya. Satu mod yang mengekalkan penghunian $0, 1, 2$ mempunyai $d = \\texttt{max\\_occupation} + 1 = 3$ aras, jadi `max_occupation >= 2` ialah keperluan yang sama dengan $d \\geq 3$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is a lower bound only: it comes from one application of the operator, and repeated application over a time evolution can reach further. It rules out cutoffs that are certainly too small, and step 6 settles, for this model and state, how large the cutoff has to be. [`mode_occupations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations\") reports the bound for each mode separately, which is what a per-mode cutoff is compared against.\n"
msgstr "Ini hanyalah had bawah: ia datang daripada satu penggunaan operator, dan penggunaan berulang sepanjang evolusi masa boleh sampai lebih jauh. Ia menolak potongan yang pasti terlalu kecil, dan langkah 6 menentukan, bagi model dan keadaan ini, seberapa besar potongan itu mesti. [`mode_occupations()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.mode_occupations\") melaporkan had bagi setiap mod secara berasingan, iaitu perkara yang dibandingkan dengan potongan per-mod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"group-before-mapping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-grouping\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Group before mapping {#2-group-before-mapping}"
msgstr "2. Kumpulkan sebelum memetakan {#2-group-before-mapping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The evolution is Trotterized, and how the Hamiltonian is partitioned decides what the synthesis is handed. Two considerations pull in the same direction.\n"
msgstr "Evolusi ini ditrotterkan, dan cara Hamiltonian dipartisi menentukan apa yang diberikan kepada sintesis. Dua pertimbangan menuju ke arah yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, a physical one: the individual hopping term $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ is **not Hermitian**. Only the pair $b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i$ is. If you evolve under a single non-Hermitian term, the operation is not unitary, and the mapped operator would carry complex coefficients that [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) rejects. Each bond’s two hopping terms must therefore stay together.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, satu yang fizikal: sebutan lompatan individu $b^\\dagger_i b_j$ **bukan Hermitian**. Hanya pasangan $b^\\dagger_i b_j + b^\\dagger_j b_i$ yang Hermitian. Jika anda mengevolusikan di bawah satu sebutan bukan Hermitian, operasi itu tidak unitari, dan operator terpeta akan membawa pekali kompleks yang ditolak oleh [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate). Oleh itu, dua sebutan lompatan bagi setiap ikatan mesti kekal bersama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second, an efficiency one: all the on-site interaction terms are diagonal in the occupation basis and mutually commute, so they can share a single group and be synthesized together. The same holds for the bonds that touch no common site. On a chain, every second bond is such a set: bonds 0 and 2 act on disjoint pairs of modes, so their hopping terms commute and can share a group, and bond 1 forms a group of its own. If you group the even and the odd bonds, you therefore need three groups, where one group per bond needs four. Fewer groups mean fewer factors, and also a shallower circuit: with the Gray code at `max_occupation = 2` the two-qubit depth is 95 against 139. The lattice decides which bonds can share a group, which is why the partition is chosen here.\n"
msgstr "Kedua, satu yang berkaitan kecekapan: semua sebutan interaksi atas-tapak adalah pepenjuru dalam asas penghunian dan saling berkomut, jadi ia boleh berkongsi satu kumpulan dan disintesis bersama. Perkara yang sama berlaku bagi ikatan yang tidak menyentuh tapak sepunya. Pada rantai, setiap ikatan kedua ialah set sedemikian: ikatan 0 dan 2 bertindak pada pasangan mod yang tidak bertindih, jadi sebutan lompatan mereka berkomut dan boleh berkongsi satu kumpulan, dan ikatan 1 membentuk kumpulannya sendiri. Jika anda mengumpulkan ikatan genap dan ganjil, anda hanya memerlukan tiga kumpulan, sedangkan satu kumpulan bagi setiap ikatan memerlukan empat. Kumpulan yang lebih sedikit bermakna faktor yang lebih sedikit, dan juga litar yang lebih cetek: dengan kod Gray pada `max_occupation = 2` kedalaman dua-qubit ialah 95 berbanding 139. Kekisi menentukan ikatan mana yang boleh berkongsi satu kumpulan, itulah sebabnya partisi dipilih di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute carries that decision into the circuit: an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate over a grouped operator decomposes into one sub-evolution per group. The partition is chosen at the bosonic level, while the lattice structure is still visible, and it survives untouched through the mapping. The [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) covers the checks a grouping should pass.\n"
msgstr "Atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") membawa keputusan itu ke dalam litar: Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") ke atas operator berkumpulan terurai kepada satu subevolusi bagi setiap kumpulan. Partisi dipilih pada peringkat bosonik, ketika struktur kekisi masih kelihatan, dan ia kekal tidak terjejas sepanjang pemetaan. [Panduan pengumpulan](grouping#grouping-explanation) merangkumi semakan yang patut dilepasi oleh sesuatu pengumpulan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every group must itself be Hermitian, which is what the preceding pairing buys. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") checks all groups in one call:\n"
msgstr "Setiap kumpulan mesti Hermitian sendiri, iaitu apa yang diperoleh daripada pemasangan sebelumnya. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") menyemak semua kumpulan dalam satu panggilan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see what each group holds, separate the groups:\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat apa yang dipegang oleh setiap kumpulan, asingkan kumpulan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The even-and-odd grouping is a choice, and the alternative is easy to measure. If you give every bond a group of its own, you need four groups, and the same circuit then costs more two-qubit depth. The depth is counted after the circuit is lowered with the Gray code at `max_occupation = 2`, which step 4 explains:\n"
msgstr "Pengumpulan genap-dan-ganjil ialah satu pilihan, dan alternatifnya mudah diukur. Jika anda memberikan setiap ikatan kumpulannya sendiri, anda memerlukan empat kumpulan, dan litar yang sama kemudian menelan kedalaman dua-qubit yang lebih tinggi. Kedalaman dikira selepas litar diturunkan dengan kod Gray pada `max_occupation = 2`, yang diterangkan oleh langkah 4:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-bosonic-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. The bosonic circuit {#3-the-bosonic-circuit}"
msgstr "3. Litar bosonik {#3-the-bosonic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note what is absent from the circuit. There is no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count. It acts on four bosonic modes:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan apa yang tiada dalam litar. Tiada pemangkasan, tiada pengekodan, dan tiada bilangan qubit. Ia bertindak pada empat mod bosonik:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A BosonicCircuit on four modes with an InitializeModes gate followed by one Evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-9.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A BosonicCircuit on four modes with an InitializeModes gate followed by one Evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-9.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The wires are bosonic modes, not qubits. Note that [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") takes **integers**, not flags: a mode can hold any number of bosons, so a Fock state is a list of occupation numbers.\n"
msgstr "Wayar ialah mod bosonik, bukan qubit. Perhatikan bahawa [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") mengambil **integer**, bukan bendera: satu mod boleh memegang sebarang bilangan boson, jadi keadaan Fock ialah senarai nombor penghunian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") turns the grouping from [step 2](#bose-hubbard-grouping) into one gate per group:\n"
msgstr "Satu [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.decompose\") menukar pengumpulan daripada [langkah 2](#bose-hubbard-grouping) kepada satu Gate bagi setiap kumpulan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The decomposed BosonicCircuit with one Evolution gate per group.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The decomposed BosonicCircuit with one Evolution gate per group.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/bose_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first group holds the bonds on modes 0 and 1 and on modes 2 and 3, so its gate spans all four modes, and so does the on-site group. The middle bond has a gate of its own on modes 1 and 2.\n"
msgstr "Kumpulan pertama memegang ikatan pada mod 0 dan 1 serta pada mod 2 dan 3, jadi Gatenya merentangi keempat-empat mod, begitu juga kumpulan atas-tapak. Ikatan tengah mempunyai Gate tersendiri pada mod 1 dan 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Skip that decomposition and the grouping is simply ignored. Which method does the splitting is the `synthesis` of the gate, with [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\") as the default; [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows the alternatives.\n"
msgstr "Langkau penguraian itu dan pengumpulan hanya diabaikan. Kaedah yang melakukan pemisahan ialah `synthesis` bagi Gate, dengan [`BosonicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-synthesis-bosonic-lie-trotter#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.synthesis.BosonicLieTrotter\") sebagai lalai; [Mensintesis Gate Evolution dalam ruang bosonik](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) menunjukkan alternatifnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Choose the encoding at transpile time {#4-choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time}"
msgstr "4. Pilih pengekodan pada masa transpilasi {#4-choose-the-encoding-at-transpile-time}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is the payoff. The same circuit is lowered four times, under four different [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") values, by changing one argument. A [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") pairs the encoding with the truncation of every mode, and the following preset derives the layout, the state preparation, and the operator mapping from that one spec (see [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)). A string such as `\"gray\"` is accepted wherever a `LevelEncoding` is.\n"
msgstr "Inilah manfaatnya. Litar yang sama diturunkan empat kali, di bawah empat nilai [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") yang berbeza, dengan menukar satu argumen. Satu [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") memasangkan pengekodan dengan pemangkasan bagi setiap mod, dan pratetap berikut menerbitkan susun atur, penyediaan keadaan, dan pemetaan operator daripada satu spesifikasi itu (lihat [Huraikan pemangkasan dengan LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)). Rentetan seperti `\"gray\"` diterima di mana-mana sahaja `LevelEncoding` diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These numbers contradict a natural guess. The unary encodings use $d$ qubits per mode against $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ for the compact codes, and at $d = 3$ the compact codes win on both axes at once: fewer qubits and far fewer entangling gates. The two unary variants differ in the operator they emit, not in their layout: [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED\") carries a projector on every other qubit of a mode, which makes it the most expensive of the four to evolve, and [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED\") leaves the projectors out and agrees with it on the one-hot subspace. The [mappers guide](mappers#unary-variants-explanation) shows the two operators side by side, and explains why the Gray code beats standard binary (SB) on the hopping terms.\n"
msgstr "Nombor-nombor ini bercanggah dengan andaian yang semula jadi. Pengekodan unari menggunakan $d$ qubit bagi setiap mod berbanding $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ bagi kod padat, dan pada $d = 3$ kod padat menang pada kedua-dua paksi serentak: qubit lebih sedikit dan jauh lebih sedikit Gate berbelit. Kedua-dua varian unari berbeza pada operator yang dihasilkan, bukan pada susun atur mereka: [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_PROJECTED\") membawa projektor pada setiap qubit selang-seli bagi satu mod, yang menjadikannya paling mahal untuk dievolusikan antara keempat-empatnya, dan [`LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.UNARY_UNPROJECTED\") meninggalkan projektor dan bersetuju dengannya pada subruang satu-panas. [Panduan mapper](mappers#unary-variants-explanation) menunjukkan kedua-dua operator bersebelahan, dan menerangkan mengapa kod Gray mengatasi binari standard (SB) pada sebutan lompatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sawaya et al. report the same ordering <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id4):\n"
msgstr "Sawaya et al. melaporkan susunan yang sama <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id4):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> though the unary code tends to require more qubits but fewer operations, it is often the case that the SB or Gray code is more efficient both in terms of qubit counts and operation counts\n"
msgstr "> walaupun kod unari cenderung memerlukan lebih banyak qubit tetapi lebih sedikit operasi, lazimnya kod SB atau Gray lebih cekap dari segi bilangan qubit dan bilangan operasi\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Their conclusion is that the best code depends on the Hamiltonian and on $d$, which is the strongest argument for not fixing the choice in the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kesimpulan mereka ialah kod terbaik bergantung pada Hamiltonian dan $d$, yang merupakan hujah terkuat untuk tidak menetapkan pilihan itu dalam litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Under a level encoding a mode spans several qubits, so the qubit register is wider than the mode register. The preset uses [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\"), which derives the register width from the [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"). The [transpilation guide](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) walks through the stages the preset runs.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Di bawah pengekodan aras, satu mod merentangi beberapa qubit, jadi daftar qubit lebih lebar daripada daftar mod. Pratetap menggunakan [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\"), yang menerbitkan lebar daftar daripada [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"). [Panduan transpilasi](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) menerangkan peringkat yang dijalankan oleh pratetap.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-against-exact-dynamics\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"bose-hubbard-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Verify against exact dynamics {#5-verify-against-exact-dynamics}"
msgstr "5. Sahkan terhadap dinamik tepat {#5-verify-against-exact-dynamics}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "None of the preceding steps establishes that the circuit is right. For that, compare the site densities $\\langle n_m \\rangle$ after evolution against an exact reference computed on the encoded Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Tiada satu pun langkah sebelumnya mengesahkan bahawa litar itu betul. Untuk itu, bandingkan ketumpatan tapak $\\langle n_m \\rangle$ selepas evolusi terhadap rujukan tepat yang dikira pada Hamiltonian terkod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reference has to be computed in the same truncated space the circuit works in, because comparing against an untruncated calculation would conflate Trotter error with truncation error, which are different things and worth separating (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Rujukan mesti dikira dalam ruang terpangkas yang sama dengan yang digunakan litar, kerana membandingkan terhadap pengiraan tanpa pemangkasan akan mengelirukan ralat Trotter dengan ralat pemangkasan, yang merupakan perkara berbeza dan wajar diasingkan (lihat [Pangkas ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With those in hand, the exact evolution in the truncated space:\n"
msgstr "Dengan itu di tangan, evolusi tepat dalam ruang terpangkas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bosons spread from the occupied end of the chain towards the empty one, and the two bosons are conserved:\n"
msgstr "Boson merebak dari hujung rantai yang dihuni ke arah yang kosong, dan kedua-dua boson terabadi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now the circuit. Note that the preceding reference was built from `initial` directly, so the circuit compared against it must contain only the evolution, because the [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate would re-prepare a state that is already prepared.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang litar. Perhatikan bahawa rujukan sebelumnya dibina daripada `initial` secara langsung, jadi litar yang dibandingkan dengannya mesti hanya mengandungi evolusi, kerana Gate [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") akan menyediakan semula keadaan yang sudah disediakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error halves as the step count doubles, which is the $O(t^2/\\text{steps})$ signature of a first-order product formula. That is the evidence that the discrepancy is Trotter error and the encoding is faithful.\n"
msgstr "Ralat menjadi separuh apabila bilangan langkah berganda, iaitu tandatangan $O(t^2/\\text{steps})$ bagi formula hasil darab peringkat pertama. Itulah bukti bahawa percanggahan ialah ralat Trotter dan pengekodan adalah setia.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The repetitions come from the `synthesis` of the gate, which Trotterizes in bosonic space where the grouping still exists: each step applies every group once, and the steps follow one another. That is different from handing a [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) with `reps > 1` to the qubit-level synthesis plugin. There, each group is already its own [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), so the formula only subdivides the terms within a group and never interleaves the groups. The groups do not mutually commute, so that leaves a single outer Trotter step whose error does not shrink however large `reps` is. [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) compares the two and covers higher orders.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Pengulangan datang daripada `synthesis` bagi Gate, yang mentrotterkan dalam ruang bosonik tempat pengumpulan masih wujud: setiap langkah menggunakan setiap kumpulan sekali, dan langkah-langkah itu berturutan. Itu berbeza daripada menyerahkan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) dengan `reps > 1` kepada pemalam sintesis peringkat qubit. Di situ, setiap kumpulan sudah menjadi [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) tersendiri, jadi formula hanya membahagikan sebutan dalam satu kumpulan dan tidak pernah menyelang-nyelikan kumpulan. Kumpulan tidak saling berkomut, jadi itu meninggalkan satu langkah Trotter luar yang ralatnya tidak mengecil sebesar mana pun `reps`. [Mensintesis Gate Evolution dalam ruang bosonik](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) membandingkan kedua-duanya dan merangkumi peringkat lebih tinggi.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The preceding [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) call is essential. [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) uses a [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate)’s exact definition and bypasses the product formula entirely. If you verify against an un-decomposed circuit, you see near-perfect agreement even for a deliberately wrong synthesis. The un-decomposed circuit also forces a dense $2^{n} \\times 2^{n}$ operator to be built, whereas a decomposed circuit applies gates one at a time. Other simulators can treat the gate differently, so this check depends on the simulator, whereas hardware always needs the decomposed form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Amaran\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Panggilan [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#decompose) sebelumnya adalah penting. [`evolve()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector#evolve) menggunakan takrifan tepat bagi [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) dan memintas formula hasil darab sepenuhnya. Jika anda mengesahkan terhadap litar yang tidak diuraikan, anda melihat persetujuan hampir sempurna walaupun bagi sintesis yang sengaja salah. Litar yang tidak diuraikan juga memaksa operator padat $2^{n} \\times 2^{n}$ dibina, manakala litar yang diuraikan menggunakan Gate satu demi satu. Simulator lain boleh memperlakukan Gate secara berbeza, jadi semakan ini bergantung pada simulator, manakala perkakasan sentiasa memerlukan bentuk yang diuraikan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, the central check: the physics must not depend on which encoding was chosen.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, semakan utama: fizik tidak boleh bergantung pada pengekodan yang dipilih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The qubit counts, Pauli structures, and circuit depths all differ, and the physics agrees to ten decimal places. The encoding is an implementation choice, which is why it belongs to the transpiler. The two unary variants agree here because the simulated state stays on the one-hot subspace; away from it they would differ.\n"
msgstr "Bilangan qubit, struktur Pauli, dan kedalaman litar semuanya berbeza, dan fizik bersetuju hingga sepuluh tempat perpuluhan. Pengekodan ialah pilihan pelaksanaan, itulah sebabnya ia milik Transpiler. Kedua-dua varian unari bersetuju di sini kerana keadaan yang disimulasikan kekal pada subruang satu-panas; di luarnya ia akan berbeza.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Truncation is a convergence parameter {#6-truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter}"
msgstr "6. Pemangkasan ialah parameter penumpuan {#6-truncation-is-a-convergence-parameter}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The final step is specific to bosons. Everything so far had fixed `max_occupation = 2`, that is $d = 3$. However, the truncation is not a free choice: it is a **convergence parameter**, and an answer is only trustworthy after it stops moving (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Langkah akhir khusus untuk boson. Semua setakat ini menetapkan `max_occupation = 2`, iaitu $d = 3$. Namun, pemangkasan bukan pilihan bebas: ia ialah **parameter penumpuan**, dan jawapan hanya boleh dipercayai selepas ia berhenti berubah (lihat [Pangkas ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit carries no truncation, so the circuit itself does not change when the cutoff does: only the transpilation is repeated. What changes is the size of what comes out, and a sweep is only as cheap as it is here because the system is tiny. The following reference is an exact classical simulation of the truncated dynamics, which is possible for four sites and grows exponentially with the number of qubits. For a problem beyond that reach there is no exact reference to compare against, and the convergence has to be judged by other means.\n"
msgstr "Litar tidak membawa pemangkasan, jadi litar itu sendiri tidak berubah apabila potongan berubah: hanya transpilasi diulang. Apa yang berubah ialah saiz hasilnya, dan sapuan hanya semurah ini kerana sistemnya kecil. Rujukan berikut ialah simulasi klasik tepat bagi dinamik terpangkas, yang mungkin untuk empat tapak dan bertambah secara eksponen dengan bilangan qubit. Bagi masalah di luar jangkauan itu tiada rujukan tepat untuk dibandingkan, dan penumpuan mesti dinilai dengan cara lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At `max_occupation = 1` ($d = 2$) each site holds at most one boson, so the interaction term, which needs two on a site, cannot act at all, and the densities are off by about $7 \\times 10^{-4}$. When you add the third level, the result captures the interaction, and from `max_occupation = 3` on the result is stationary to machine precision: converged.\n"
msgstr "Pada `max_occupation = 1` ($d = 2$) setiap tapak memegang paling banyak satu boson, jadi sebutan interaksi, yang memerlukan dua pada satu tapak, tidak boleh bertindak langsung, dan ketumpatan tersasar kira-kira $7 \\times 10^{-4}$. Apabila anda menambah aras ketiga, hasilnya menangkap interaksi, dan dari `max_occupation = 3` seterusnya hasilnya pegun hingga ketepatan mesin: bertumpu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reason that it stops at `max_occupation = 2` is particle number. The Hamiltonian conserves the number of bosons, and this state holds two, so no site can ever hold more than two, whatever the evolution time and whether the interaction is repulsive or attractive. If you evolve to $t = 6$ instead of $t = 0.4$, or flip the sign of $U$, the densities at `max_occupation = 2` and higher stay unchanged to $10^{-13}$.\n"
msgstr "Sebab ia berhenti pada `max_occupation = 2` ialah bilangan zarah. Hamiltonian mengabadikan bilangan boson, dan keadaan ini memegang dua, jadi tiada tapak boleh memegang lebih daripada dua, walau apa pun masa evolusi dan sama ada interaksi bersifat tolakan atau tarikan. Jika anda mengevolusikan hingga $t = 6$ dan bukannya $t = 0.4$, atau menterbalikkan tanda $U$, ketumpatan pada `max_occupation = 2` dan lebih tinggi kekal tidak berubah hingga $10^{-13}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What does push the requirement up is the **number of bosons**. Three bosons on the same chain change by about $2 \\times 10^{-3}$ between `max_occupation = 2` and `3` after the same short evolution, and by about $0.3$ after $t = 6$. That is a statement about this model and a conserved quantity, and it is a bound only for operators that conserve the particle number; it is not a general rule, so the cutoff has to be swept, not guessed.\n"
msgstr "Apa yang benar-benar menaikkan keperluan ialah **bilangan boson**. Tiga boson pada rantai yang sama berubah kira-kira $2 \\times 10^{-3}$ antara `max_occupation = 2` dan `3` selepas evolusi pendek yang sama, dan kira-kira $0.3$ selepas $t = 6$. Itu ialah pernyataan tentang model ini dan kuantiti terabadi, dan ia hanya had bagi operator yang mengabadikan bilangan zarah; ia bukan peraturan am, jadi potongan mesti disapu, bukan diteka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sweep has a price on the circuit side too, which is what the exact reference does not show. The same bosonic circuit, lowered with the Gray code at each cutoff:\n"
msgstr "Sapuan juga ada harganya di sisi litar, yang tidak ditunjukkan oleh rujukan tepat. Litar bosonik yang sama, diturunkan dengan kod Gray pada setiap potongan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each extra level costs depth, and the qubit count jumps whenever $d$ passes a power of two. When you converge in $d$, you therefore trade accuracy against circuit size, so the sweep is more than a numerical check.\n"
msgstr "Setiap aras tambahan menelan kedalaman, dan bilangan qubit melonjak setiap kali $d$ melepasi kuasa dua. Apabila anda menumpu dalam $d$, anda justeru menukar ketepatan dengan saiz litar, jadi sapuan lebih daripada sekadar semakan berangka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note also that $d = 2$ being nearly right is a coincidence of the observable: the site *densities* barely move, while the underlying state is qualitatively wrong (it has no doubly-occupied component). If one observable converges, that does not show that another has converged.\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan juga bahawa $d = 2$ hampir betul ialah satu kebetulan bagi cerapan: *ketumpatan* tapak hampir tidak bergerak, manakala keadaan asasnya salah secara kualitatif (ia tiada komponen berpenghunian dua). Jika satu cerapan menumpu, itu tidak menunjukkan bahawa cerapan lain telah menumpu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Apa yang perlu diambil {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The encoding is a transpiler concern.** The bosonic circuit in [step 3](#bose-hubbard-transpile) mentions no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count. Four encodings then lowered it to four different circuits, all reproducing the same physics. Nothing upstream of the transpiler had to change.\n"
msgstr "**Pengekodan ialah isu Transpiler.** Litar boson dalam [langkah 3](#bose-hubbard-transpile) tidak menyebut pemotongan, pengekodan, mahupun bilangan qubit. Empat pengekodan kemudian menurunkannya kepada empat litar yang berbeza, semuanya menghasilkan semula fizik yang sama. Tiada apa-apa di hulu Transpiler yang perlu diubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**For bosons this is not merely convenient.** The truncation is a convergence parameter that has to be swept, and it lives inside the encoding. A circuit built against a fixed encoding would have to be rebuilt for every value of $d$.\n"
msgstr "**Bagi boson, ini bukan sekadar memudahkan.** Pemotongan ialah parameter penumpuan yang perlu disapu, dan ia terletak di dalam pengekodan. Litar yang dibina berdasarkan pengekodan tetap perlu dibina semula untuk setiap nilai $d$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Group before mapping, and group for Hermiticity.** A single hopping term is not Hermitian and cannot be exponentiated; the bond pair on the hand is Hermitian and therefore can be exponentiated. Decide the partition at the bosonic level, where the lattice is still visible. That is physically necessary, and the [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") attribute exists to carry the decision forward.\n"
msgstr "**Kumpulkan sebelum pemetaan, dan kumpulkan demi kehermitan.** Satu sebutan lompatan tunggal tidak Hermitian dan tidak boleh dieksponenkan; pasangan ikatan pula Hermitian dan oleh itu boleh dieksponenkan. Tentukan pembahagian pada peringkat boson, di mana kekisi masih kelihatan. Itu perlu secara fizikal, dan atribut [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.groups\") wujud untuk membawa keputusan itu ke hadapan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Do not assume the low-weight encoding is the cheap one.** At $d = 3$ the compact codes beat both unary variants on qubits and gates simultaneously, and the projected variant is the costliest of all. Measure; the crossover is $d$-dependent.\n"
msgstr "**Jangan anggap pengekodan berpemberat rendah ialah yang murah.** Pada $d = 3$ kod padat mengalahkan kedua-dua varian unari dari segi qubit dan gate serentak, dan varian terunjur ialah yang paling mahal. Ukur; titik silangnya bergantung pada $d$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Truncation breaks the algebra, in a quantifiable way.** Only on the top retained level, by $d$. That is also why mapping does not commute with normal ordering.\n"
msgstr "**Pemotongan merosakkan aljabar, secara yang boleh dikuantifikasikan.** Hanya pada aras teratas yang dikekalkan, sebanyak $d$. Itulah juga sebabnya pemetaan tidak berkomutasi dengan tertib normal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two directions extend this example. If you replace the chain’s edge list with the bonds of a square lattice, you need no other change, because the `bose_hubbard` function defined earlier is already geometry-agnostic. A custom encoding of your own (a block-unary code, for example, which interpolates between unary and compact) also plugs in through the same `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` seam the preset uses.\n"
msgstr "Dua arah memanjangkan contoh ini. Jika anda menggantikan senarai tepi rantai dengan ikatan kekisi segi empat sama, anda tidak perlu mengubah apa-apa lagi, kerana fungsi `bose_hubbard` yang ditakrifkan sebelum ini sudah tidak bergantung pada geometri. Pengekodan tersuai anda sendiri (contohnya kod unari-blok, yang menginterpolasi antara unari dan padat) juga boleh disambungkan melalui sambungan `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` yang sama yang digunakan oleh pratetap.\n"

